  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p>At 948 feet, <strong>Pinnacle</strong> is a summit in Indiana. The Pinnacle Trail covers 2.0 miles round trip (out-and-back) with about 217 feet of elevation gain \u2014 a gradual walk with modest climbing.</p>\n  <h3>The Route</h3><p>Most of the climbing comes early \u2014 the first half of the route does the bulk of the work before the grade eases. The steepest stretch arrives around mile 0.5, gaining roughly 1,100 feet per mile \u2014 expect a slow, deliberate pace through here. From the trailhead at about 781 feet, the route tops out near 942 feet.</p>\n  <h3>Getting There</h3><p>The trailhead is at <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=38.86707,-85.99939\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">38.86707, -85.99939</a> (tap for driving directions). It's roughly 190 miles north of Nashville, Tennessee. Arrive early on weekends \u2014 trailhead lots at popular peaks fill quickly, and cell service is often unreliable once you leave the highway.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>Spring through fall is the main season. Conditions change fast in the shoulder months \u2014 check a point forecast for the summit, not the nearest town, before you commit.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>The Easy rating comes from the National Park Service difficulty formula, which weighs total distance against elevation gain. Most hikers should budget about 1.0 hours of moving time; add margin for breaks, photos and the descent. Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include Hominy Mortar, Pikes Peak and Hounds Leap \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
